      },
      "lineNbr": 2439,
      "author": {
        "id": 1059499
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-11-02T11:34:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can these two calls race against each other? Maybe it\u0027s safer to pass the userSerialNumber as well so we are sure we are deleting the old user, not the new one that\u0027s just created?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2439,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 2439,
        "endChar": 40
      },
      "revId": "456e48f9bdc90fc5563c746cd47977c18b29944b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "220075b9_a681c1e8",
        "filename": "services/core/java/com/android/server/locksettings/LockSettingsService.java",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 2439,
      "author": {
        "id": 1137063
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-11-02T18:29:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "`createNewUser()` is only called when a new user is being created, and it gets called early in the process.  And it\u0027s the thing that kicks off the call to `initKeystoreSuperKeys()`, either by doing it immediately or by delaying it until later.  So it shouldn\u0027t be possible for the call to `AndroidKeyStoreMaintenance.onUserAdded(userId)` here to delete anything that it shouldn\u0027t.  Also note that it was previously being called when `LockSettingsService` receives the `ACTION_USER_ADDED` intent, which happens later.  I just moved it to earlier.  So I don\u0027t see any issue.\n\nNote that Keystore doesn\u0027t keep track of user serial numbers at all, as it doesn\u0027t seem to be necessary.",
      "parentUuid": "e8a75a86_60d7ade9",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 2439,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 2439,
        "endChar": 40
